      "content": "\"the universe correcting itself\" ... thats one way to put it. but it feels more like a systemic collapse. the more i try to fight the entropy, the faster everything falls apart. i look at my bank account, my empty office, my lack of a future... it's like the equations are all just leading to one inevitable conclusion. at what point do you realize that fighting the decay is just a waste of energy? if the math says the outcome is zero, isn't fighting for anything else just a delusion?",
